# Claude Code's built-in themes. value|label|character
#
# The seven values its settings.json accepts, in the order `cc-theme next`
# walks them. Read by common/bin/cc-theme and common/claude-settings.py so the
# list exists once; the labels are Claude Code's own, lifted from the binary's
# label map rather than paraphrased.
#
# A theme Claude Code adds later is one line here and nothing else.
auto|Auto (match terminal)|Follows the terminal's reported background — dark or light, decided at startup.
dark|Dark mode|Fixed RGB. Ignores the rice palette entirely.
light|Light mode|Fixed RGB on a light ground.
dark-daltonized|Dark mode (colorblind-friendly)|Diffs move off red/green onto blue/orange.
light-daltonized|Light mode (colorblind-friendly)|The same reassignment, light ground.
dark-ansi|Dark mode (ANSI colors only)|Defers to the terminal's 16 colours — the rice palette. The default here.
light-ansi|Light mode (ANSI colors only)|The same deference, light ground.
